    "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nThe BIP-346 reference implementation in `bip-0346/ref-impl` accepts truncated long-form `TxFieldSelector`s.\r\n\r\n`calculate_txhash` parsed the global byte and the input/output-fields byte, then treated the **input** and **output** selection bytes as optional: when absent it defaulted to an empty selection (NONE). As a result:\r\n\r\n- a 2-byte selector `[global, fields]` was silently treated as input=NONE, output=NONE\r\n- a 3-byte selector `[global, fields, input-selector]` was silently treated as output=NONE\r\n\r\nThis invents NONE semantics the spec does not define. bip-0346.md states (\"For both inputs and then outputs, expect an additional byte\") that both selection bytes belong to the long form, and the `OP_TXHASH` precondition requires the `TxFieldSelector` to be valid, failing otherwise.\r\n\r\n## Change\r\n\r\nMake the input and output selection bytes mandatory in `calculate_txhash`, returning an error when they are missing. The generated test vectors (`txhash_vectors.json`) and the vector generator were updated to use explicit 4-byte long-form selectors; all 150 `txhash` values are unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- Added `reject_truncated_long_form_txfs` regression test (2-byte and 3-byte selectors are rejected; an explicit 4-byte NONE/NONE selector is accepted).\r\n- `cargo test` passes; `cargo run` regenerates the vectors with identical hashes.\r\n",
